course: dictionary
lesson: 15976
title: Upfront: early money and honest talk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Upfront has two meanings. The first is about money: to pay upfront means to pay before you get the thing you are buying. «The shop wants the full price upfront, before it sends your bike.»
explain: The second meaning is about people. An upfront person is honest and open, and says things clearly, even when the truth is not nice. «Mia was upfront: she told us the cake had burnt before anyone took a bite.»
explain: To work out which meaning is right, read the words around it. If the sentence is about paying, ask: before or after? If it is about talking, ask: honest or hiding something? You can also write it as two words, up front: «Please tell me up front if you can't come.»
fact: Upfront is an adjective and an adverb. It can also be written as two words: up front.
fact: «Upfront» about money means paid or done before the goods or work are received.
fact: «Upfront» about people means honest and open about things.
fact: Useful phrases: pay upfront, and be upfront about something.
fact: A quick check: in money talk, ask "before or after?"; in people talk, ask "honest or hiding it?"
exercise: «We had to pay upfront for the tickets.» What does upfront mean here? | Free of charge | *Paid before we got them | Paid in small coins | Paid after the show ended
exercise: Kai says, «I'll be upfront: I didn't do my homework.» What does upfront mean? | Loud and happy | Very late | *Honest and open | Hidden under the bed
exercise: «The shop asks you to pay upfront for the sofa.» Find and copy the word that tells you the money is paid early. | asks | sofa | *upfront | shop
test: Ava says, «Please be upfront about how you feel.» What does be upfront mean? | Forget it | Shout it across the room | *Say it honestly and clearly | Keep it secret
test: «The builders want half the money upfront.» When is the money paid? | Never | *Before the work starts | Halfway through the job | After the house is finished
exam: «The website says delivery is free, but you must pay upfront.» What does upfront mean here? | *Paid before the parcel arrives | Paid after the parcel arrives | Not paid at all | Paid by a friend
